hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16064","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, he said, al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili narrated to me, he said, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing upon his mount on the day of sacrifice at Mina."
"16065","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar, and he is al-Ijli, narrated to us, al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili narrated to us, he said, I was riding behind my father on the day of sacrifice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing upon his she-camel at Mina."
"16066","Abd Allah ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said, Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed me, from al-Hirmas, he said, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a camel toward Syria."
"16067","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Imran ibn Abi Ali Abu Muhammad, of the people of Rayy, and his origin was Isfahani, narrated to us, he said, Yahya ibn al-Durays narrated to us, he said, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Hirmas, he said, I was riding behind my father, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a camel, and he was saying: Here I am, with a pilgrimage and an umrah together."
